{
 "about": "CC1 sweep of Long (Rachm.) against plain Long, 2026-10-09 (branch violas-rachm-curve): is Violas Long (Rachm.)'s dip between CC1 64 and 89 in the shipped dynamics calibration real? Windows test VM, real SSO in Kontakt 8 (the All techniques patches Violas and Violins 1 at library defaults, MuseScore's resaved setups), offline renders through kthost at 44.1 kHz. Each note: CC32 = the switch, CC11 127 and CC1 = x 1.0 s before the note-on, velocity = x (as Check articulations > Dynamics plays its curve), held 1.0 s, a note every 3.5 s (the 0.3 s before each note-on at -95 dB or less). x = 40, 42 .. 110 at each pitch, three renders: x ascending, descending, shuffled; each value is their median. Long (Rachm.) has one round robin: the three renders gave identical numbers (range 0.00-0.01 dB). Plain Long alternates two round robins: up to 3.2 dB (1.2 at pitch 69) and up to 670 Hz of centroid apart, so its medians mix them.",
